                  "type": "application",
                  "title": "Apply It: HIM Operations Crosswalk to These Laws",
                  "content": "Each statute imposes specific operational duties on HIM. Use this crosswalk:\n\n**HITECH Breach Notification:**\n• Maintain breach risk assessment template (4-factor)\n• 60-day individual notification clock; 60-day HHS reporting for 500+\n• Annual aggregate HHS report for <500\n• Document de-identification methodology\n\n**Cures Act Information Blocking:**\n• Map all access workflows (patient, payer, provider-to-provider)\n• Set policy to default to access; document any exception invoked\n• Train ROI staff on 8 exceptions and required documentation\n• Audit response times to API/portal access requests\n• Eliminate blanket clinician-hold policies on lab/imaging results\n\n**MACRA/MIPS PI:**\n• Annual reporting period planning (Jan-Dec)\n• Extract eCQM data from EHR for quality category\n• Document Improvement Activities completion\n• Ensure information blocking attestation = YES\n• Coordinate with quality department on measure selection\n\n**Promoting Interoperability (Hospital):**\n• Annual EHR Incentive program reporting via QualityNet\n• Track public health data exchange engagement (immunization, ELR, syndromic)\n• Update SAFER Guides annually\n\n**Part 2 / CARES Act:**\n• Update SUD consent forms to new template by Feb 16, 2026\n• Train ROI on new single-consent-for-TPO model\n• Maintain redisclosure prohibition notice\n• Extend breach notification protocols to Part 2 records\n\n**DSCSA (Pharmacy):**\n• Verify TI/TH/TS for incoming drug shipments\n• Maintain saleable return verification logs\n• Coordinate suspect-product investigations",
