                  "explanation": "Under TJC Standard MS.08.01.01, FPPE (Focused Professional Practice Evaluation) is REQUIRED whenever a practitioner is initially granted privileges — this is one of the three FPPE triggers (the others being a new privilege requested by an existing practitioner, and a concern arising during OPPE). FPPE is time-limited and uses specific competency criteria appropriate to the privilege (chart review, proctoring, simulation, or external peer review). Only AFTER successful completion of FPPE does the practitioner transition to OPPE — Ongoing Professional Practice Evaluation (MS.08.01.03), which is continuous review typically conducted every 6 months. This applies even to board-certified, experienced practitioners because TJC's framework requires individualized validation in THIS facility's context (different patient population, EHR, surgical team, equipment). NPDB query is separately required at initial appointment AND every 2 years thereafter under HCQIA — but is not an 'evaluation process,' it's a database check.",
