                  "explanation": "Option B is the **five-habit pattern** that integrates legal grounding (statutes), ethical reasoning (principles), professional standards (AHIMA), accountability (documentation), and institutional process (escalation). It is the only combination that satisfies **OCR**, **AHIMA Professional Ethics Committee**, **personal liability** (both civil under FCA and criminal under HIPAA), and **professional integrity**. Deference (option A) abandons the duty under AHIMA Code Principle IV. Refusal to act in gray areas (option C) fails patients and may itself be unethical and noncompliant (information blocking). Trusting counsel without documenting (option D) creates the very paper-trail gap that destroys later defenses. The credentialed HIM professional is the one who can show their reasoning, on paper, every time.",
